    /* S_SEC_HELP */ "Help",
    /* S_TITLE_HELP */ "Help",
    /* S_SUB_HELP */ "A open  B back  X search",
    /* S_SUB_HELP_TOPICS */ "A select  B back",
    /* S_SUB_HELP_ARTICLE */ "B back",
    /* S_GETTING_STARTED */ "Getting started",
    /* S_HELP_HOWTO */ "How-To",
    /* S_HELP_TROUBLESHOOTING */ "Troubleshooting",
    /* S_REPLAY_TOUR */ "Replay the guided tour",
    /* S_HELP_SEARCH */ "Search",
    /* S_TITLE_HELP_SEARCH */ "Search Help",
    /* S_HELP_SEARCH_GUIDE */ "Search Help (e.g. \"emulator folder\", \"box art\")",
    /* S_SUB_HELP_SEARCH */ "A open  Y new search  B back",
    /* S_HELP_SEARCH_NO_RESULTS */ "Nothing matched that search. Try fewer or different words, or browse Getting Started, How-To, and Troubleshooting instead.",
    /* S_TOUR_NEXT */ "Next",
    /* S_TOUR_BACK */ "Back",
    /* S_TOUR_CLOSE */ "Close",
    /* S_TOUR_DONE */ "Get started",
    /* S_TOUR1_TITLE */ "Welcome to HaulNX",
    /* S_TOUR1_BODY */ "HaulNX is a ROM management app for your Switch. Organize your library by console, verify files are good, and keep your emulators pointed at the right folders. You can also browse curated archive.org collections to fill gaps with legitimate homebrew, public-domain, and preservation content.\n\nThis quick tour covers the essentials. Replay it any time from Settings > Help.",
    /* S_TOUR2_TITLE */ "Your Library",
    /* S_TOUR2_BODY */ "Library is your management home: every installed game, grouped by console, with Verify, Tidy, and box art tools.\n\nSwitch between tabs with L/R, or the tab bar at the top.",
    /* S_TOUR3_TITLE */ "Building your library",
    /* S_TOUR3_BODY */ "Pick a console then a repository to see its files. Press X to select several at once, then A to queue everything you picked in one go.\n\nQueued items download in the background, so you're free to keep browsing while they run.",
    /* S_TOUR4_TITLE */ "The Queue tab",
    /* S_TOUR4_BODY */ "Queue lists every active and pending transfer in one place: downloads, files pushed from a PC, and app/emulator updates. Press A on an item to cancel it.",
    /* S_TOUR5_TITLE */ "Point your emulators at your library",
    /* S_TOUR5_BODY */ "Games install to sdmc:/roms/<console> by default. Most emulators need to be told to look there: set each emulator's ROM folder to match, or do the reverse and give a console its own custom install folder in Settings > Storage > Install Folders if an emulator expects its own path.\n\nGet this right once and every future download just shows up.",
    /* S_TOUR6_TITLE */ "Keeping your library healthy",
    /* S_TOUR6_BODY */ "Settings > Data Files can verify your games against known-good checksums (DAT files) and flag anything missing or corrupt. Settings > Storage lets you tidy up misfiled or duplicate files, console by console.\n\nBox art, card vs. list view, and what's using your SD card space all live in Appearance and Storage too.",
    /* S_TOUR7_TITLE */ "The PC companion",
    /* S_TOUR7_BODY */ "The free HaulNX desktop app connects over Wi-Fi (via the always-on inventory server) or USB to move files both ways, back up your collection, and manage emulators, with no SD card shuffling.\n\nFind it under Settings > PC Sync. And remember: Settings > Help has How-To guides and Troubleshooting whenever you need them.",
    /* S_TOUR8_TITLE */ "The Collections tab",
    /* S_TOUR8_BODY */ "Collections lists every console HaulNX supports. Each one can point at one or more repositories you can browse: curated sources for legitimate homebrew, public-domain, and preservation content.\n\nPress X on a console, then Add Repo, to add one by archive.org item ID or a direct URL.",
    /* S_TOUR_QUEUE_MOCK_NAME */ "Homebrew Demo (USA).z64",
    /* S_GS1_TITLE */ "What HaulNX does",
    /* S_GS1_BODY */ "HaulNX is a ROM management app first, a downloader second: it organizes your installed games by console, verifies them against checksums, cleans up misfiled or duplicate files, fetches box art, and keeps emulators and apps updated.\n\nBrowsing curated archive.org repositories to fill gaps in your library is one part of that, not the whole app.",
    /* S_GS2_TITLE */ "Point your emulators at your library",
    /* S_GS2_BODY */ "By default, games install to sdmc:/roms/<console> — a plain folder per console (Settings > Storage shows the exact path). Set each emulator's ROM path to match, or use Settings > Storage > Install Folders to give a console its own custom path instead if an emulator expects one.\n\nDo this once per emulator and new downloads just appear where it expects them.",
    /* S_GS3_TITLE */ "Adding your first collection",
    /* S_GS3_BODY */ "You need at least one repository before there's anything to browse.\n\nFrom Add, press Y to add a repository, or use the desktop companion (Settings > PC Sync) to send a ready-made collection over Wi-Fi or USB.",
    /* S_GS4_TITLE */ "Where your downloads go",
    /* S_GS4_BODY */ "Downloaded archives extract straight into your ROM folder automatically, unless you turn on Keep Archives Compressed in Settings > Downloads.\n\nAnything that lands without a clear match sits in the Inbox (Settings > Storage) until you sort it.",
    /* S_GS5_TITLE */ "Finding your way around Settings",
    /* S_GS5_BODY */ "Settings is organized by task: Appearance, Downloads, Storage, Data Files, PC Sync, Account, Updates, Logs, Diagnostics, and this Help section.\n\nEach row opens a single-purpose screen — nothing is buried more than one level deep.",
    /* S_GS6_TITLE */ "Getting help later",
    /* S_GS6_BODY */ "Come back to Settings > Help any time: How-To covers everyday tasks like adding art or updating emulators, and Troubleshooting walks through common problems and fixes.\n\nYou can also replay the guided tour from the row above.",
    /* S_HOWTO1_TITLE */ "Add a repository",
    /* S_HOWTO1_BODY */ "From Add, press Y (or a console's Options menu) to add a repository by archive.org item ID or a direct download URL.\n\nYou can also use Search (the magnifying glass) to search archive.org's catalogue and add a matching item directly.",
    /* S_HOWTO2_TITLE */ "Download multiple games at once",
    /* S_HOWTO2_BODY */ "In a repository's file list, press X on a file to select it, then keep selecting more — a running count and total size shows at the bottom. Press A once to queue everything selected together.\n\nSettings > Downloads controls how many run at once and any rate limits, if downloads feel too fast or too slow.",
    /* S_HOWTO3_TITLE */ "Point your emulators at your ROM folder",
    /* S_HOWTO3_BODY */ "Games install to sdmc:/roms/<console> by default (Settings > Storage shows the exact path). Point each emulator's ROM folder setting there.\n\nIf an emulator insists on its own folder instead, turn on Settings > Storage > Install Folder Mode (custom) and set that one console's path under Console Folders — HaulNX will install there instead, no manual copying.",
    /* S_HOWTO4_TITLE */ "Download DAT files and verify your library",
    /* S_HOWTO4_BODY */ "Settings > Data Files > Manage DAT Files downloads the checksum sets used to verify games.\n\nFrom a console's Options menu in Library, choose Verify Files to check every installed game against its DAT — bad, unknown, or misnamed files are listed with a fix offered where possible.",
    /* S_HOWTO5_TITLE */ "Tidy a messy library",
    /* S_HOWTO5_BODY */ "From a console's Options menu in Library, choose Tidy Library to scan for misfiled and duplicate files. Each finding lists a suggested fix — review one at a time, or apply everything at once.",
    /* S_HOWTO6_TITLE */ "Add box art for consoles and games",
    /* S_HOWTO6_BODY */ "From a console's Options menu in Library, choose Scan for Box Art to fetch covers for everything installed at once.\n\nOn a single game, open its Options menu and pick a cover manually if the automatic match isn't right, or if you just want a different one.",
    /* S_HOWTO7_TITLE */ "Change how your library looks",
    /* S_HOWTO7_BODY */ "Settings > Appearance switches between card and list view, groups games by console or shows them flat, and sets the accent color and light/dark theme.\n\nBox Art and Auto-Fetch Box Art are separate toggles there too — turn either off if you'd rather keep things fast and plain.",
    /* S_HOWTO8_TITLE */ "Change the app's language",
    /* S_HOWTO8_BODY */ "Settings > Appearance > Language lists every language HaulNX ships with. Pick one and the whole app updates immediately — no restart needed.",
    /* S_HOWTO9_TITLE */ "Choose which consoles show",
    /* S_HOWTO9_BODY */ "Settings > Sources (or Appearance) > Manage Consoles lets you show or hide any console on Browse and Library independently — hide ones you don't use without deleting their repos or configuration.",
    /* S_HOWTO10_TITLE */ "Update your emulators and apps",
    /* S_HOWTO10_BODY */ "Settings > Updates > App & Emulator Updates lists everything with an update source configured, shows installed vs. latest version, and installs or reverts a build in place.\n\nSet a source first (X on an entry) if one isn't configured yet.",
    /* S_HOWTO11_TITLE */ "Prefer one version per game (1G1R)",
    /* S_HOWTO11_BODY */ "Settings > Storage > DAT Files hosts the 1G1R region-preference order — set which region wins when the same game exists in several regions, then Verify or Tidy applies it.",
    /* S_HOWTO12_TITLE */ "Move a game to another console folder",
    /* S_HOWTO12_BODY */ "Open a game's Options menu (X) in Library and choose Move — pick the destination console and it's relocated (and re-verified if you have DATs for it).",
    /* S_HOWTO13_TITLE */ "Free up space: clear out folders",
    /* S_HOWTO13_BODY */ "Settings > Storage > Manage Downloads clears the scratch folder used mid-download; Manage Inbox clears anything that landed without a clear match.\n\nLargest Files lists your whole library's biggest files first, so you know exactly what to remove if space is tight.",
    /* S_HOWTO14_TITLE */ "View logs and export a debug bundle",
    /* S_HOWTO14_BODY */ "Settings > Logs holds the download history, debug log, queue state, transfer log, and speed-test log — each viewable and clearable on its own.\n\nExport Debug Bundle folds all of them into one file to attach to a bug report.",
    /* S_HOWTO15_TITLE */ "Connect the PC companion over Wi-Fi",
    /* S_HOWTO15_BODY */ "Turn on the inventory server in Settings > PC Sync, then open the HaulNX desktop app on the same network — it finds your console automatically and can push or pull files, back up your collection, and manage emulators, all without a cable.",
    /* S_HOWTO16_TITLE */ "Connect over USB",
    /* S_HOWTO16_BODY */ "Settings > Diagnostics > USB File Transfer turns your console into a USB drive the desktop app (or any MTP-capable file manager) can browse and transfer to — cable-only, no Wi-Fi needed.",
    /* S_HOWTO17_TITLE */ "Search your library and repositories",
    /* S_HOWTO17_BODY */ "The magnifying glass in Library searches installed games; in Add it searches across every repository you've added; and in a console's file list it searches archive.org's catalogue for that console.",
    /* S_HOWTO18_TITLE */ "Back up and restore your collection setup",
    /* S_HOWTO18_BODY */ "HaulNX automatically keeps the last two versions of your console/repository configuration. Settings > PC Sync > Restore Collection brings one back if an import or edit went wrong.",
    /* S_HOWTO19_TITLE */ "How unzipping and extraction work",
    /* S_HOWTO19_BODY */ "By default, a downloaded archive (zip/rar/7z) extracts straight into the right console folder automatically and the archive itself is deleted once it lands — you never handle a zip file by hand.\n\nTurn on Keep Archives Compressed (Settings > Downloads) to keep new downloads zipped instead, trading a bit of convenience for less used space and a slightly longer install step in your emulator.\n\nAnything that finishes downloading but doesn't clearly match a console sits in the Inbox (Settings > Storage) unextracted until you sort it by hand.",
    /* S_HOWTO20_TITLE */ "Add your Archive.org, GitHub, and SteamGridDB credentials",
    /* S_HOWTO20_BODY */ "Settings > Account Credentials holds three separate, optional pieces of login:\n\n• Archive.org Access/Secret Key — needed only for items that require a logged-in archive.org account to download. Generate a pair at archive.org/account/s3.php and enter both under Archive.org Credentials.\n\n• GitHub API Token — raises how often HaulNX can check GitHub for emulator/app/DAT updates before being rate-limited. A free personal access token with no special scopes is enough; generate one at github.com/settings/tokens.\n\n• SteamGridDB API Key — lets box-art scans pull higher-quality art. Get a free key at steamgriddb.com/profile/preferences/api.\n\nAll three are stored on the console and never required just to browse or download public items.",
    /* S_HOWTO21_TITLE */ "What's in each Settings section",
    /* S_HOWTO21_BODY */ "Appearance — theme, accent color, card vs. list view, box art.\nDownloads — extraction, rate limits, keep-archives-compressed, inbox handling.\nFilters — which file types repositories show.\nStorage — free space, biggest folders, custom console install folders.\nPC Sync — the desktop companion: Wi-Fi/USB transfer, install from PC, restore a backed-up collection.\nAccount Credentials — optional Archive.org/GitHub/SteamGridDB logins (see the credentials article).\nUpdates — check for and install HaulNX, emulator, and app updates.\nData Files — download DAT sets used by Verify.\nLogs / Diagnostics — activity log, network self-test, USB transfer toggle, debug bundle export.\nHelp — this hub, and the guided tour.",
    /* S_HOWTO22_TITLE */ "Set a custom install folder for a console",
    /* S_HOWTO22_BODY */ "Games install to sdmc:/roms/<console> by default. If an emulator expects its own path instead, open Settings > Storage > Install Folders and switch it from Default to Custom Per Console, then pick the console and choose any folder on the SD card as its install location.\n\nVerify, Tidy, and box art all keep working normally against the new folder. The change only applies to new downloads; anything already installed under the old path needs moving by hand.",
    /* S_HOWTO23_TITLE */ "Control download speed and concurrency",
    /* S_HOWTO23_BODY */ "Settings > Downloads has three knobs for how downloads behave:\n\nMax Simultaneous Downloads sets how many run at once (higher isn't always faster on a slow connection).\nMax Total Download Rate caps combined throughput across every active download.\nMax Rate Per Download caps each one individually, useful for keeping one big download from starving the others.\n\nAll three default to unlimited/1. Set any rate to 0 to remove that cap.",
    /* S_HOWTO24_TITLE */ "Hide file types you don't want to see",
    /* S_HOWTO24_BODY */ "Open Settings > Appearance > File Extension Filter to hide specific file types from repository listings and downloads, such as extras, artwork, or manuals that sometimes ship alongside a ROM.\n\nToggle the master switch on, then add an extension (Y) and toggle it on to start hiding it. Turning an individual extension off keeps it in the list without hiding it, so you can re-enable it later without re-adding it.",
    /* S_TS1_TITLE */ "No network at startup",
    /* S_TS1_BODY */ "HaulNX warns if it can't reach the internet when it starts. Retry once you're connected, or Continue to browse anything already cached — downloading and browsing repositories both need a connection.\n\nTurn this check off in Settings > Diagnostics if you often use HaulNX offline.",
    /* S_TS2_TITLE */ "Downloads are stuck or failing",
    /* S_TS2_BODY */ "Check Settings > Diagnostics > Network Self-Test for a quick connectivity check, and Speed Test to measure real throughput.\n\nA download rate limit set too low (Settings > Downloads) can also look like a stall — try raising or clearing it.",
    /* S_TS3_TITLE */ "The PC companion won't connect over Wi-Fi",
    /* S_TS3_BODY */ "Confirm the inventory server is on (Settings > PC Sync) and both devices are on the same network — the companion can't find a console across different Wi-Fi networks or through a guest network with client isolation.\n\nWaking the console from sleep can take a few seconds to reconnect; give it a moment and refresh.",
    /* S_TS4_TITLE */ "Nothing shows up over USB",
    /* S_TS4_BODY */ "Turn on USB File Transfer in Settings > Diagnostics, then reconnect the cable — some cables are power-only. If the PC still doesn't see it, check the USB 3.0 status row in Settings > Diagnostics and try a different port.",
    /* S_TS5_TITLE */ "Verify reports Bad or Unknown files",
    /* S_TS5_BODY */ "Bad means the file doesn't match its DAT checksum — a corrupted or incomplete download; re-download it. Unknown means no DAT entry matched it — the DAT set may be out of date; fetch the latest from Settings > Data Files.",
    /* S_TS6_TITLE */ "Can't verify a console (no DAT)",
    /* S_TS6_BODY */ "Not every console has a DAT set available. Settings > Data Files > Manage DAT Files shows what's downloadable — if a console isn't listed there, verification isn't supported for it yet.",
    /* S_TS7_TITLE */ "An emulator or app update failed",
    /* S_TS7_BODY */ "Settings > Updates > App & Emulator Updates shows the failure reason (offline, rate-limited, or no source set). Set or fix the source (X on the entry) and try again — Revert restores the previous backup if a bad install landed.",
    /* S_TS8_TITLE */ "Running low on SD card space",
    /* S_TS8_BODY */ "Settings > Storage shows free space and the biggest files in your library. Turning on Keep Archives Compressed (Settings > Downloads) keeps new downloads zipped instead of extracted, trading space for a slightly longer install step.",
    /* S_TS9_TITLE */ "An import from the PC didn't bring anything in",
    /* S_TS9_BODY */ "Make sure you're sending from the same screen that generated the address/code shown — it's a one-time session. If it timed out, back out and start the import again from Settings > PC Sync.",
    /* S_TS10_TITLE */ "\"Restart to update\" but nothing happens",
    /* S_TS10_BODY */ "An update finishes installing on the next full restart, not just returning to the home menu — close HaulNX completely (hold X on it, or use the Home Menu) and relaunch it.",
    /* S_TS11_TITLE */ "My emulator can't find my games",
    /* S_TS11_BODY */ "Check Settings > Storage for the exact ROM folder path and point your emulator there — the default is sdmc:/roms/<console>, unless a custom install folder is set for that console.\n\nA custom folder only applies to new downloads; games already installed elsewhere need moving by hand (or with Move, from a game's Options menu, if it's another console HaulNX manages).",
    /* S_TS12_TITLE */ "Box art isn't showing",
    /* S_TS12_BODY */ "Check Settings > Appearance > Box Art is turned on. If it is, run Scan for Box Art from a console's Options menu — a game with an unusual title may need a manual match from its own Options menu instead.",
    /* S_TS13_TITLE */ "An archive downloaded but won't extract",
    /* S_TS13_BODY */ "Check Settings > Storage first — a full SD card fails extraction partway through and leaves a partial file behind. Delete the partial and free up space, then re-download; a corrupted archive extracts cleanly once the download itself is good.\n\nIf it keeps failing with space to spare, turn on Keep Archives Compressed (Settings > Downloads) as a workaround and extract it yourself later with a PC archive tool.",
    /* S_TS14_TITLE */ "GitHub rate limit hit",
    /* S_TS14_BODY */ "GitHub caps how many unauthenticated checks HaulNX can make per hour — shared across every HaulNX user on the same public IP, so it can trigger even on a first-time check. Add a free GitHub API token in Settings > Account Credentials to raise the limit (see the credentials article), or just wait — it resets on its own within the hour.",
    /* S_TS15_TITLE */ "Archive.org says the item needs a login",
    /* S_TS15_BODY */ "Some archive.org items are only downloadable to a logged-in account. Generate an Access/Secret Key pair at archive.org/account/s3.php and enter both in Settings > Account Credentials > Archive.org Credentials, then retry the download.",
    /* S_TS16_TITLE */ "Downloads are slower than expected",
    /* S_TS16_BODY */ "Check Settings > Downloads for a rate limit left over from a previous session — Max Total Download Rate and Max Rate Per Download both default to unlimited, but either one being set low will cap every download.\n\nIf both are clear, run Speed Test in Settings > Diagnostics to see what your connection is actually delivering right now.",
    /* S_TS17_TITLE */ "A file type isn't showing in Library",
    /* S_TS17_BODY */ "Settings > Appearance > File Extension Filter can hide specific file extensions from repository listings. Open it and check whether the master switch and the extension in question are both toggled on — turn either off to stop hiding it.",
    /* S_TS18_TITLE */ "The first-run tour or Welcome screen won't come back",
    /* S_TS18_BODY */ "Both only appear automatically on a fresh install, once. Replay the guided tour any time from Settings > Help > Getting Started > Replay the Guided Tour — it ends on the same Welcome screen you saw the first time.",
    /* S_VERIFY_DAT */ "Verify Files",
